<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in October.</title>
<headline>RTRS-Australia building approvals rise in October.</headline>
<dateline>CANBERRA 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Australian dwelling unit building approvals rose a seasonally-adjusted 12.8 percent in October to 11,121 from 9,861 in September, compared with 10,000 in October 1995, the Australian Bureau of Statistics said.</p>
<p>Economists on average had expected building approvals to rise 5.0 percent.  </p>
<p>Australian housing building approvals-</p>
<p>    SEASONALLY ADJUSTED		   Oct 96   Sept 96  Oct 95</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  6,741     7,200   7,024</p>
<p>    Total houses			     6,886     7,346   7,188</p>
<p>    Total private dwelling units	10,549     9,428   9,400</p>
<p>    Total dwelling units		  11,121     9,861  10,000</p>
<p>    Value residential building (A$ bln) 1.25	1.14   1.14</p>
<p>    Value total buildings (A$ bln)	2.39	2.29   2.11</p>
<p>TREND ESTIMATES</p>
<p>    Private Sector Houses		  6,946     6,970   7,205</p>
<p>    Total Dwelling Units		  10,622    10,534  10,326</p>
<p>The bureau said the seasonally adjusted number of private sector houses approved in October fell by 6.4 percent, while the number of other residential dwelling units approved rose by 68.4 percent, which was its highest level since March 1995.</p>
<p>The value of non-residential building, which has been particularly strong in recent months, fell 16.8 percent to A$1.06 billion seasonally adjusted, and was 2.9 percent higher in trend terms on September.</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
